#: ../../source/user_guide/templates.rst:286
msgid ""
"Once ``params`` is declared -- even naming a single key -- it is the "
"**complete** parameter set: none of ``title``/``authors``/``date``, "
"``papersize``/``fontsize``/ ``lang``, or the ``toctree_*`` keys arrive "
"unless the ``params`` dict names them itself. This example's ``params`` "
"dict names only ``subtitle``, ``version`` and ``confidential``, so "
"exactly those three named parameters reach the template above -- its "
"``title`` parameter keeps its own default (``\"\"``) because nothing ever"
" passes it a value. See :doc:`configuration`'s precedence section for the"
" full exclusivity rule."
msgstr ""

